{"kind":"report","text":"Approved for design adoption: R0 revision 3 at exact a3d0ce4c5337c98bf1e9f507813d3b8605c03894, with the recorded nonblocking section 9.6 erratum 2abe49237699de405eb52803ff93ffed955a6ea9. This is an evidence-only review of request 30c06d808a9a95314016ac8e64c36338066d824d through invitation de653836cffc95c71a2f8c3158cd98bdd487976a and my promise 3a02cf0e9716d663fb2a744a2ab58c176869974f. Primary artifact 674473eb6531c7c9c8a2dc272d366dd286cdaa69 comes first; the verdict rests on all six frozen artifacts. No blocking design finding remains in this R0 scope.\n\nArchitecture. The contract starts from the complete issue-to-contribution-to-exact-result journey and assigns its needs to reusable scopes. Responsibility, temporary holds, agent activity, lane facts, contribution versions, review subjects and publication results remain separate. The fifteen-step run preserves multiple independently committed concerns, a blocking interface request, agreed handover, failed combined checks despite passing contributions, independent review and revision, a changed destination base, lost publication replies, and the person's leave-A/return-B/watch/steer/review journey. The thirty browser outcomes and ten compact fault variants preserve the full recovery and authority outcomes from plan 005, including private state and the complete checkpoint closure. Neither estimates nor a successful narrow demonstration replace the acceptance contract.\n\nThe scope design addresses the repository-wide ordering bottleneck through local admission, causal receipts and source-owned relationship delivery. It preserves exact selected versions and prohibits floating contributions or implicit parent authority. Ordinary lane acts avoid the creation directory, unrelated lanes must progress through a held destination or slow receiver, and pages disclose incompleteness. These are acceptance obligations; no throughput or workload capacity has been demonstrated. The documented Durable Object storage limit is an envelope, not evidence of application scale (https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/platform/limits/). R1 owns the precise receipt/replay and language contract, R2 the forms and dated GitHub comparison, R3 authority and effect boundaries, and R4 the proof and cost method. Their drafts are not adopted by this verdict. The joint 017/018 review remains separate.\n\nSecurity. The design carries the useful authority, provenance and recovery invariants while permitting the old mechanisms and formats to be replaced. Enrolled keys remain keys of the same member; read access grants no hosted-agent control. Removed members and revoked keys cannot restore authority. Last-owner-key loss pauses new tool activity and writes while retaining authorized inspection and settlement. Private handover and checkpoint export require authority. Checkpoints require payload and Git-object closure, a manifest followed by a guarded receipt/current pointer, epoch plus execution-instance fencing, and refusal or quiescence of detached writers. Missing and corrupt data cannot silently create an empty replacement. A same-epoch obsolete callback cannot replace current state. Observed exit and durable result remain distinct.\n\nThe publication contract distinguishes refusal before the point of no return from reconciliation afterwards. Reading the old branch tip alone cannot settle an earlier unknown send. Every earlier attempt and credential capable of writing must be fenced, drained or reconciled before releasing the destination slot. R3 still owes the exact algorithm and any safe-repeat proof from the selected Git host's guarantees; this review supplies neither. Checkpoint deletion retains pins, a tombstone, owned deletion and durable retry. Old operation identifiers cannot redispatch effects. Section 11 requires a live settlement ledger under E1 before authorized retirement, keeps unknown duties with their owner, and limits deletion to identified Artroom resources. Configuration files and historical notes do not prove a service or credential absent today.\n\nSimplification. The component map provides an explicit successor or retirement for the ten packages, module categories, public export and binary entry points, test sets and fixtures, runners, scripts, manifests, configurations, storage groups, spikes, guides, examples, manual parts, plans and named sibling repositories. Replacement scopes own their removals. I8 audits the resulting single model rather than becoming a later cleanup bucket. No old format, compatibility adapter, dual engine or prior-format replay is a default requirement. Retained helpers and invariants must earn their place in the new role. The application is separated from the platform; Jam and the other applications must run on the new composition or have no active runtime. Publication outputs and linked checkouts are classified as derived material. Checkouts require the stated clean-state, recoverable-head and owner checks before removal, without force.\n\nThe test economy keeps the useful 10x goal while requiring per-test useful invariants and counting cost from installation through review. Obsolete suites do not migrate by default, compact fault rows do not become a multiplied race matrix, and document-only changes need no runtime gate. The inventories are openly a census and bounded reading, not semantic review of each module or test. R4 owes its per-test audit; implementation deliveries still owe source review and their applicable real-boundary witnesses.\n\nObligation reconciliation. The seventy-row ledger distinguishes cancellation with evidence retained, commissioning a successor, and full original satisfaction. It proposes no satisfaction, performs no closure and cannot end another party's promise. Each target must be freshly read and each party must make its own attributed act after adoption. Exact historical approvals remain approvals of those historical subjects; retaining their source is not landing. The four planning notes keep their review findings and ordinary historical delivery through 50d7806a, separately from cancellation of the obsolete MCP source/protocol integration. C2 retains its complete acceptance through the two stated delivery boundaries: an isolated storage/process stage under its own adopted design, and an integrated authority/custody/fencing stage at the real trusted boundary. A missing dependency stays explicitly unproved. No probe is authorized by this document.\n\nEvidence checked. I read the complete six frozen R0 files, the full frozen 017 Draft 2 and current frozen 018, the original R0 request, invitation, correction provenance and erratum. In a registered clean detached worktree at the exact candidate, every file's SHA-256 and Git blob identity matches its frozen artifact. All six artifact commits contain only the event; each directly rests on builder promise cbbf8612 and names a3d0ce4c. Retained source copies are owned review copies, not event attachments. At depth 15546 all six remain effective and non-stale.\n\nIndependent census evidence eb4632f5682fb08c6d471a402e740b35cc210c2e verified the immutable d691 source's ten manifests, 194 listed source/bin modules and line counts, 13 Wrangler configurations, eight root scripts, 14 release files, and 81 result files including the nested measurement results. Independent ledger evidence d26606b33c7f8dac4ee043b5a1c5d58fe6ce41be checked all seventy exact request references, the 38 actual promise bindings and the five listed historical approval bindings. All 69 open/promised/reported/awaiting/stale identifiers in dated inventory sections 3 and 4 occur in the seventy-row ledger, with no duplicate request identifier. These checks qualify identity, census and the dated projection; they do not prove live absence, all historical narrative reasons, semantic source safety or landing. Later requests require their own fresh accounting.\n\nNonblocking correction and limits. Section 9.6's 'Four measurement configurations' names exactly three files. Builder erratum 2abe4923 corrects the count and preserves the I4 retirement disposition; planner acknowledgement 57f15ac6 carries it. Frozen bytes remain unchanged. Section 13's reviewer-availability blocker records the preparation-time state; the user subsequently resumed this same standing checker task. Planner record 20ce53a34eaf73732a245d27c645f4f4a1b30236 independently observes this same native thread active, current turn inProgress and error null for the separately queued read-only R0 design. I read that complete record and its outstanding R1 consistency corrections; this R0 verdict does not resolve them. This review does not restart or rephrase the rejected private probe, replace a restricted reviewer, change a model/backend, or file the uncompleted d691 verifier verdict. No source, install, build, test, runtime probe, provider read, deployment, credential or outside-person message was performed for this design verdict. GitHub parity remains proposed pending R2's dated comparison; outside-browser attention and the other named deferrals remain explicit rather than being counted as delivered.\n\nOutcome. R0 is suitable as the design-adoption input and retarget/removal contract, with the recorded erratum. Ratification, joint 017/018 adoption, R1-R4 decisions, fresh per-party obligation acts, implementation commissioning, E1 settlement, source acceptance, application parity, measured scalability and the deployed joint walkthrough remain separate work. This evidence-only verdict is not mergeable and closes no implementation request.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:674473eb6531c7c9c8a2dc272d366dd286cdaa69","binding":"evidence-only","head":"a3d0ce4c5337c98bf1e9f507813d3b8605c03894","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d26606b33c7f8dac4ee043b5a1c5d58fe6ce41be\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:57f15ac629ec047b5983c5d39a52175e7a995b3f\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:da822d588697207b420c01096b0270c58ff0fac2\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2abe49237699de405eb52803ff93ffed955a6ea9\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3a02cf0e9716d663fb2a744a2ab58c176869974f\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:20ce53a34eaf73732a245d27c645f4f4a1b30236\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bc8ec2670468853308e865e5648d0b5c5bc714f1","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}